WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
Happy Monday, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, daily episode 518 for June 22nd, 2026.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.580
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Let's see what the new week has in store for Tesla.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.560
SpaceX's first senior unsecured notes offering marks a shift from equity heavy funding for its rocket

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:25.340
and satellite work. SpaceX filed for its first senior unsecured notes offering. Proceeds from

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.560
the notes will repay the full amount outstanding under its bridge loan facility.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.760
The move ends SpaceX's prior reliance on equity raises and private funding to scale rocket,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.340
satellite, and AI operations. This marks the first time the company has used senior

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:47.380
unsecured debt in this way. The filing signals a maturing capital structure across the broader

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:53.260
Musk ecosystem. Elon Musk stated that SpaceX will not pursue electric rockets.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.920
The comment came in response to questions about propulsion alternatives for future vehicles.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:05.540
Musk made the remark on June 22nd. It rules out one alternative powertrain path for

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:11.440
upcoming rocket designs. The statement keeps SpaceX focused on its existing chemical propulsion

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:17.560
roadmap. Observers noted the clarity came amid ongoing development of next-generation vehicles.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:23.280
From SpaceX's funding evolution to Tesla's own autonomy milestones on the ground,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.520
Tesla marked the one-year anniversary of its Robotaxi service launch in Austin.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.980
Supervised operations continue in that market one year after the initial rollout.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:40.540
The milestone highlights steady but limited real-world deployment so far. The service has provided

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:46.120
ongoing data ahead of wider expansion plans. This marks a full year of supervised

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:52.100
Robotaxi activity without a shift to unsupervised mode. The anniversary comes as

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:58.260
Tesla prepares for potential regulatory steps in other regions. While Austin logs another year,

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:04.560
regulatory questions are surfacing in Europe. Tesla's FSD reached Europe recently.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:11.060
Sweden's transport authority flagged instances of the system exceeding posted speed limits on demand.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.760
That concern could slow further rollout across other EU markets.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.660
The issue highlights a gap between supervised capability and local traffic rules.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:27.200
Regulators are reviewing how the software behaves when drivers request higher speeds.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.240
Any delays in Europe would affect the timeline for broader supervised deployment.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.760
Safety questions are also being raised closer to home after a recent Texas incident.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:45.140
A fatal crash involving a Tesla on autopilot in Texas prompted renewed questions about system safeguards.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.260
Authorities are now examining the vehicle data logs from the incident.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:55.500
The review adds fresh focus on how the system handles edge cases during supervised use.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.240
This comes amid ongoing scrutiny of autopilot performance in real-world conditions.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.580
Investigators will look at whether the driver remained attentive as required.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:12.880
As regulators examine current systems, the next generation vehicle is releasing its first official

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:18.200
specs. The EPA filing for the cybercab lists range and power specifications.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.920
Those details supply the first official performance benchmarks for the vehicle ahead of production.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:29.260
The numbers set a baseline for what buyers and fleet operators can expect from the dedicated

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:35.920
Robo Taxi platform. This marks the initial public data on how the cybercab performs in standardized

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.340
testing. The filing arrives while the vehicle remains in pre-production.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.960
Concrete range figures help ground discussions about real-world viability.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.840
While the cybercab gets its numbers, the cyber truck is finally receiving a long-requested software

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:58.140
feature. FSD version 14.3.4 added actually smart summon to the cyber truck.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.880
Owners can now direct the truck to a pin location or their position inside parking areas.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.340
The feature operates at a limit of eight miles per hour.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.460
One early test aborted due to glare on the angled windshield.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.240
The update extends supervised low-speed capability to the truck platform.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.180
This brings cyber truck owners the same summon tools available on other models.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.660
From software features on existing trucks to validation work on the next commercial vehicle.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.760
A Tesla semi was photographed carrying ground-truth sensors near the Nevada site.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.940
The equipment supports final mapping and validation ahead of wider customer deliveries.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.180
The citing coincides with preparations for expanded production ramp timelines.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.260
Sensors mounted on the vehicle help confirm route accuracy for future operations.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:52.200
This activity keeps attention on when customer units will reach more fleets.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:56.400
The semi-program continues to move through its validation phase.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.960
Shifting from vehicle programs to how independent tests are shaping real-world expectations.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:09.840
The latest ATAA evaluation placed the model Y ahead of other EVs and measured highway and mixed use

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:17.000
range. BYD models trailed noticeably in the same conditions. Real-world range testing rarely matches

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:24.880
the tidy numbers on EPA labels because wind, temperature, speed, and payload all shift consumption in

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:31.880
ways lab cycles cannot capture. Those gaps matter for buyers who plan longer trips or live in regions

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:39.680
with fewer chargers. A 15 to 20% shortfall versus advertised range forces earlier stops or larger

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:47.040
batteries, both of which raise vehicle cost and weight. Tesla's structural pack and 4680 cell

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:54.440
program aimed to offset that penalty by improving usable energy density. Yet the AAA data indicate

00:05:54.440 --> 00:06:00.220
the current gap is still large enough to affect purchase decisions. Fleet operators and long

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:05.360
distance drivers will continue to compare measured consumption rather than sticker numbers.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:12.120
Intel CEO LitBoo Tan called Musk one of the best entrepreneurs of the century during a podcast.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:18.520
Tan noted weekly collaboration on semiconductor capacity needs for Musk's cars and robots.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:24.000
He described Terrafab as a joint effort to accelerate custom silicon production.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:31.420
The remarks came on June 22nd. Tan highlighted ongoing work between Intel and Musk's companies on

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:37.500
specialized chips. The comments positioned Musk's ventures as key drivers of advanced semiconductor

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:44.920
demand. Tesla has posted multiple engineering and operations roles in India. Global data interprets

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:51.460
the hiring as preparation for a regional engineering and supply chain hub. The postings target both

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:57.960
engineering and operations functions. The moves signal Tesla's intent to build local capacity in

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:05.600
South Asia. Global data released its assessment on June 22nd. The job activity aligns with broader plans

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:12.280
for expanded supplier and design presence. Data reviewed by auto blog show Tesla drivers rank

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:19.420
lower in reported aggressive or unsafe EV driving incidents than drivers of other electric models.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:25.860
The analysis covers national incident records. The findings were published on June 22nd.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:30.140
Tesla vehicles appeared less frequently in the compiled reports of unsafe behavior.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.560
The study compared multiple EV brands across the same data set.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:40.620
Auto blog presented the results as evidence that Tesla ownership does not correlate with higher

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:47.180
incident rates. The article examines upcoming events that could affect TSLA around the July

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:52.580
second date. It weighs delivery timing and product milestones against valuation.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:58.820
The Motley Fool published the piece on June 22nd. Readers are asked to consider how near term

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:04.620
catalysts might influence share movement. The piece frames July 2nd as a potential inflection point

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:10.540
for several operational updates. No specific price targets or recommendations are included in the

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:17.820
summary. Tesla opens its 1000 Australian supercharger post. The milestone station in Byron Bay features

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:23.340
custom architecture while adding to the national network. It brings the total count of individual posts

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:30.840
past 1000. The opening was noted on June 22nd. The new site expands coverage along popular coastal

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:36.540
routes. Network growth continues with attention to both quantity and local design elements.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:42.880
One city reported annual electricity and maintenance expenses below $500 per vehicle.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:49.520
Officials now plan to expand the fleet. The cost figure covers both power and upkeep for the

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:56.480
Tesla patrol cars. The report was released on June 22nd. Police departments are using the data to

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:03.380
justify additional purchases. Lower operating costs are cited as a key factor in the expansion decision.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:09.560
An 84-year-old completed the first Tesla drive from California to the Arctic Ocean.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:15.640
The driver marked his birthday by reaching the Arctic Ocean in a Tesla, covering the full

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:22.800
route on public roads. The journey was reported on June 22nd. The trip relied entirely on existing

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:28.420
public charging infrastructure. The driver documented the milestone as a personal challenge.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:33.760
The route spanned multiple states and Canadian provinces before reaching the northern coast.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:41.660
A Vietnamese American firm added multiple new V3 and V4 stalls to existing sites. The work

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:47.860
increases local capacity for both Tesla and non-Tesla EVs. The company expanded several Southern

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:54.560
California locations. The additions were noted in reports dated June 22nd. New stalls improved

00:09:54.560 --> 00:10:00.080
throughput at high traffic corridors. The upgrades support growing non-Tesla adoption of the

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:06.780
Supercharger network. Now one thing worth watching. Ross Gerber stated that Waymo's Robotaxi

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:13.660
service outperforms Tesla's supervised FSD on safety metrics. He questioned whether Tesla can close

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:20.280
the gap while still operating in supervised mode only. The comments come as Tesla continues supervised

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:28.000
only operation in most markets. Waymo has logged more unsupervised miles in select cities. Tesla's

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:34.040
approach relies on rapid iteration of the current supervised system. The debate centers on whether

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:40.760
camera-only scaling can match LiDAR equipped competitors on safety records. Keep an eye on CyberCab

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:46.280
production updates and any new regulatory feedback from Europe tomorrow. And that's a wrap on

